  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing (NAICS 339112) has $840M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $715M in FY2026 to date. The industry recorded 8,942 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $94K. Obligations fell 47.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show volatility across recent years: FY21 totaled $2.3B, FY22 totaled $1.1B, FY23 totaled $1.5B, FY24 totaled $2B, FY25 totaled $1.6B, and FY26 totaled $840M. The Department of Defense obligated $58M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $47.7M in FY2026 to date. Vendor concentration is notable: SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC received $138M, FIRST NATION GROUP LLC received $97.6M, and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC received $80.1M. MEDICAL PLACE INC, MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP, and others also appear among the largest vendors. Contractors evaluating opportunities should note the heavy VA weighting in current obligations and the mix of large vendor awards when considering competitive positioning or teaming.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is buying within this NAICS code?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for a large share of FY2026 to date obligations with $715M. The Department of Defense follows with $58M and the Department of Health and Human Services follows with $47.7M. Other agencies record smaller totals, showing high buyer concentration in VA and a modest spread across several other federal buyers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors lead federal contracting in NAICS 339112 this fiscal year to date?",
        "body": "SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC leads vendors with $138M in obligations in FY2026 to date. FIRST NATION GROUP LLC and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC follow with $97.6M and $80.1M respectively. MEDICAL PLACE INC, MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP, and SCRIPTPRO USA INC appear among the next-largest recipients."
      }
    ]
  },
